83 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371532 1084 #uuid "054e2dc4-0eee-5242-a290-5434283aac5a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371533 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371534 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371533 1069 "q-105895" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371533 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371533 1071 "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨-1,0,x{y}^{3}⟩$ and the scalar field $f(x,y,z)=yz.$ Given that\n\n$$\n∇\\times F=⟨3x{y}^{2},-{y}^{3},0⟩,\\,∇f=⟨0,z,y⟩,\n$$\n\ncalculate $∇\\times (f\\,F)$ at the point $(0,-1,2).$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371533 1072 #uuid "b8abe39b-bb92-55f7-bb84-89cdb536b574" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371533 1074 "We shall use the following identity:\n\n$$\n∇\\times (f\\,F)=f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute $∇f\\times F.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f\\times F & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & z & y \\\\ -1 & 0 & x{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =[z(x{y}^{3})-y(0)]i-[0(x{y}^{3})-y(-1)]j+[0(0)-z(-1)]k \\\\  & =xz{y}^{3}\\,i-y\\,j+z\\,k \\\\  & =⟨xz{y}^{3},-y,z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F) & =f∇\\times F+∇f\\times F \\\\  & =yz⟨3x{y}^{2},-{y}^{3},0⟩+⟨xz{y}^{3},-y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3xz{y}^{3},-z{y}^{4},0⟩+⟨xz{y}^{3},-y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4xz{y}^{3},-z{y}^{4}-y,z⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\times (f\\,F)(0,-1,2) & =⟨4(0)(2)(-1)^{3},-2(-1)^{4}-(-1),2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371534 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371535 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371534 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371536 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371534 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371537 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371534 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371538 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371534 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371539 13194139533450 17592186