501e9-e0e1-52e4-a6fd-99c98b442493" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371540 1074 "A partition of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{0,5,10},{15,20,25,…,100}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{0,5,10},{20,25,30…,100}}$ is not a partition because the element $15$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${∅,{0,5,10,…,100}}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- ${{0,5,10},{35,40,15…,100}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements (such as $20$) that do not appear in $A.$\n\n- ${{0,5,10},{10,15,20…,100}}$ is not a partition because the element $10$ appears in multiple subsets." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371542 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371543 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371544 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371545 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371546 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371544 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371541 1080 #uuid "ef1229cf-b304-57e4-adb2-c9a52b35185f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371542 1081 "{∅,{0,5,10,…,100}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371542 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371542 1084 #uuid "483a58bb-3472-593c-a4f5-040afe4273b6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371543 1081 "{{0,5,10},{35,40,15…,100}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371543 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371543 1084 #uuid "dece85ae-583e-50ca-bc85-f5825f207c11" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371544 1081 "{{0,5,10},{15,20,25,…,100}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371544 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371544 1084 #uuid "7bff6bb8-133f-5f08-8876-7f4db16f6074" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371545 1081 "{{0,5,10},{20,25,30…,100}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371545 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371545 1084 #uuid "8e6220ad-9ad9-5836-935f-e008160b7ebc" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371546 1081 "{{0,5,10},{10,15,20…,100}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371546 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371546 1084 #uuid "f53afe73-4103-5bed-84fd-c71c64afdfa5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371547 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371548 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371547 1069 "q-107424" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371547 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371547 1071 "Write the complex number $z=3-2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371547 1072 #uuid "639174e2-def8-51a3-8fdb-1422e7d1fb7d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371547 1074 "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-2}{3})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{2}{3})| \\\\  & ≈5.695.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\theta =5.695$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.695\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371549 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371550 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371551 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371552 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371553 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371549 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371548 1080 #uuid "f763ad28-1041-57dd-a12d-abdb91776047" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371549 1081 "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.695\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371549 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371549 1084 #uuid "06ded7d8-8a52-56e0-92dd-56bf1b4982bc" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371550 1081 "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.861\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371550 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371550 1084 #uuid "d71450dc-5d1e-5834-a5df-07213c49ca30" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371551 1081 "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.695\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371551 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371551 1084 #uuid "99cce532-6b2e-5ded-bfd5-fcc6a3d835d1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371552 1081 "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.976\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371552 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371552 1084 #uuid "0f7eebd9-21c6-575e-9ebb-1ec30bf3209f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371553 1081 "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.861\\,\\text{i}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371553 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371553 1084 #uuid "b606d4cf-f381-567a-b5bf-b6e8a384922e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371554 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371555 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371554 1069 "q-109003" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371554 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371554 1071 "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some integer $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+y=-\\frac{x}{y}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371554 1072 #uuid "972cc08b-2d79-5a95-8b03-a6f20f3836b7" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371554 1074 "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=-x,\\,n=-1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by $y,$ and we get\n\n$$\ny\\frac{dy}{dx}+{y}^{2}=-x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=2y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-x\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+2z=-2x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=-2x.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371556 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371557 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371558 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371559 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371560 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371558 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371555 1080 #uuid "a50b330c-f87d-5c0a-8d36-ef8cd39ea565" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371556 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371556 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371556 1084 #uuid "6d1dd27a-f2d1-518f-aaf0-11391043ab60" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371557 1081 "\\frac{2}{x}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371557 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371557 1084 #uuid "35c9a700-5e24-5f4b-b032-0cb7cd2d879c" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371558 1081 "-2x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371558 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371558 1084 #uuid "8358d758-0e97-5f01-bb8e-0c3fae7282d5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371559 1081 "-\\frac{1}{2x}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371559 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371559 1084 #uuid "39d2841c-04ce-50b3-9951-6e0a2fd427d0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371560 1081 "-2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371560 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371560 1084 #uuid "4dd4eee5-51a0-5f94-ab98-a8758174a582" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371561 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371562 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371561 1069 "q-109326" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371561 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371561 1071 "Consider the arc of the curve $x=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{12}+\\frac{1}{y}$ that lies between the lines $y=1$ and $y=e.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371561 1072 #uuid "59c768e0-123a-5f86-b9a6-1b397e77b597" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371561 1074 "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${y}_{1}=1$ to ${y}_{2}=e.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{{y}^{3}}{12}+\\frac{1}{y})=\\frac{{y}^{4}-4}{4{y}^{2}}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}=\\frac{{y}^{8}-8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{y}^{8}-8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y\\sqrt{\\frac{{y}^{8}+8{y}^{4}+16}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\,y\\sqrt{\\frac{({y}^{4}+4)^{2}}{16{y}^{4}}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}y(\\frac{{y}^{4}+4}{4{y}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}\\frac{{y}^{4}+4}{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{\\int }_{1}^{e}({y}^{3}+\\frac{4}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}{(\\frac{{y}^{4}}{4}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)\\,|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{2}(\\frac{{e}^{4}}{4}+4-\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{8}({e}^{4}+15).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371563 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371564 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371565 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371566 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371567 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371566 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371562 1080 #uuid "cfb25814-53f0-5252-8e81-2248d22b22d0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371563 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{15}({e}^{4}+1)" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371563 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371563 1084 #uuid "e775560f-3f4c-54be-841d-b0c3d21fd878" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371564 1081 "\\frac{4\\pi }{15}({e}^{4}-12)" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371564 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371564 1084 #uuid "32562cc2-5b04-5833-b156-51f71e7dd7ca" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371565 1081 "\\frac{\\pi {e}^{2}}{4}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371565 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371565 1084 #uuid "deec031c-a589-562b-a505-50630bb393d6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371566 1081 "\\frac{\\pi }{8}({e}^{4}+15)" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371566 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371566 1084 #uuid "5fd98cc9-8e2e-5c55-8146-376a748259e0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371567 1081 "\\frac{\\pi {e}^{4}}{32}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371567 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371567 1084 #uuid "4d694888-90d9-5e06-bcb4-c0145a723e0c" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371568 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371569 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371568 1069 "q-110152" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371568 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371568 1071 "The first term of a geometric series is $5,$ the last term is $5\\,120,$ and the common ratio is $2.$ What is the sum of this series?\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the fact that $1\\,024={2}^{10}.$*" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371568 1072 #uuid "20d592ca-19e9-5a78-8362-355e1f68cc3d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371568 1074 "Given a geometric series, the sum of the first $N$ terms is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}={a}_{1}\\frac{(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r},\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term of the series and $r$ is the common ratio. In our case, we have ${a}_{1}=5$ and $r=2.$\n\nWe must determine $N$ (the index of the last term). To do this, we use the fact that\n\n$$\n{a}_{N}={a}_{1}\\cdot {r}^{N-1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\,120 & =5\\cdot {2}^{N-1} \\\\ 1\\,024 & ={2}^{N-1} \\\\ {2}^{10} & ={2}^{N-1} \\\\ 10 & =N-1 \\\\ N & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, if we substitute ${a}_{1}=5,$ $r=2$ and $N=11$ into the formula for ${S}_{N},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{11} & =5\\cdot \\frac{1-{2}^{11}}{1-2} \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1-{2}^{11}}{(-1)} \\\\  & =5({2}^{11}-1) \\\\  & =10\\,235.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371570 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371571 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371572 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371573 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371574 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371572 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371569 1080 #uuid "2b7b3d07-2303-5be7-a53a-a2e82251759d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371570 1081 "15\\,523" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371570 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371570 1084 #uuid "4d60e7c5-6e55-5ec0-8d21-31ba4e9c1b2b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371571 1081 "12\\,035" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371571 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371571 1084 #uuid "b13e8bdd-ec12-5df2-80e3-b69a1f30bb13" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371572 1081 "10\\,235" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371572 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371572 1084 #uuid "dc23586f-f760-55b6-8483-d18036f3dc03" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371573 1081 "10\\,245" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371573 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371573 1084 #uuid "d24f9581-bc4f-52eb-95e4-9dc7c94070d5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371574 1081 "13\\,205" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371574 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371574 1084 #uuid "918e4c7b-54d0-54e3-af29-b58063794f51" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371575 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371576 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371575 1069 "q-111251" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371575 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371575 1071 "The random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x,y)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y<X<Y+2).$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371575 1072 #uuid "821858ee-46eb-57a4-9f6b-cec1ae6e7ca5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371575 1074 "If $f(x,y)$ is a joint probability density function for the random variables $X$ and $Y$ and $A⊂{R}^{2},$ then\n\n$$\nP((X,Y)\\in A)={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nNotice that $f(x,y)$ is nonnegative in the region $D=[0,3]\\times [0,1],$ and the event $A={Y<X<Y+2}$ corresponds to a subset of $D,$ shown as the shaded region below:\n\n![](images/f4/f4a0cc357eee835c84ef08524d27e3c30b98d58e1b6b5083b7df6a66ce987b6b.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<X<Y+2) & ={∬}_{A}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∬}_{A}\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\text{Area}(A) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371577 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371578 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371579 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371580 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371581 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371577 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371576 1080 #uuid "63d8ef8e-e282-5085-bd0c-37645c87d08b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371577 1081 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371577 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371577 1084 #uuid "58338181-f5f2-53c4-ba2c-1eea5f78b0ec" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371578 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371578 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371578 1084 #uuid "51c241d2-b827-5429-8bbc-12cb2e50febb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371579 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371579 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371579 1084 #uuid "08d78c40-67ca-5552-bfbc-85ea24759319" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371580 1081 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371580 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371580 1084 #uuid "6cfd8f25-4f0e-55fd-8077-79f56797ab4f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371581 1081 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371581 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371581 1084 #uuid "94df0702-4a0f-564a-b2f1-d0fd90b62b07" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371582 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371583 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371582 1069 "q-115291" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371582 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371582 1071 "![](images/84/84f42ca72c2a96a5ba03ca790bc3f0a6f6f5e582791aaf50e434bff16f77aed5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371582 1072 #uuid "639049a5-6ce8-54a1-b632-ccaefc836643" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371582 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at 