 1081 "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371587 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371587 1084 #uuid "0e59ed04-5761-52ab-a71d-01bb8815f1e8" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371588 1081 "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371588 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371588 1084 #uuid "9018af77-6271-5372-98ce-5f050e312969" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371589 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371590 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371589 1069 "q-115303" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371589 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371589 1071 "![](images/16/160ce22bf1c4bd47fbe3e2ec1391bd212a376d93b4c3a640821d28d1e0cc518f.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371589 1072 #uuid "7d5d4f0a-0454-5deb-bf0e-354930b4e862" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371589 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(0,-4),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371591 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371592 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371593 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371594 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371595 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371592 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371590 1080 #uuid "ba0a6189-0e52-5212-859c-9ea6a09989b1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371591 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{3}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371591 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371591 1084 #uuid "af2bad0e-9dc9-5968-88dc-a1e321f073c9" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371592 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371592 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371592 1084 #uuid "8c7b4737-1592-5599-866c-fb9337333c5f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371593 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371593 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371593 1084 #uuid "bcfa9944-4565-597f-8530-0793ce6c6f94" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371594 1081 "\\frac{(x-4)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371594 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371594 1084 #uuid "9afb9836-3f0b-5f92-8cd5-a659d33b2905" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371595 1081 "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{6}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371595 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371595 1084 #uuid "d60530b3-3e54-5d62-bffa-836a75315c2a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371596 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371597 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371596 1069 "q-115930" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371596 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371596 1071 "The area of a square decreases at a rate of $56{\\text{ m}}^{2}\\text{/s}.$ At what rate are the lengths of the sides of the square decreasing when the sides are $8\\text{ m}$ long?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371596 1072 #uuid "332ede8a-b7d8-56ae-b05d-98854e11eb9d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371596 1074 "Here, the area is changing at a constant rate,  and we want to know the rate at which the side lengths are changing.\n\nFirst, let's draw a diagram:\n\n![](images/1c/1cb323f4c38bb4fc13ffc81f47544424872480b42f033032da47c04d097e8696.png)\n\nWe want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ The area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know from the given information that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-56\\text{ m}{}^{2}\\text{/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information, we reach\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-56 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{28}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, when the sides are $8\\,\\text{m},$ we have $x=8.$ Substituting this information into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{28}{8}=-\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the lengths of the sides are decreasing at a rate of $\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371598 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371599 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371600 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371601 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371602 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371599 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371597 1080 #uuid "c59fb865-44ed-5cc4-bf4d-8ff775b26354" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371598 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371598 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371598 1084 #uuid "fad524f3-747b-543d-877c-19d0bc18ff69" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371599 1081 "\\frac{7}{2}\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371599 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371599 1084 #uuid "d1d8801c-f0ce-5902-a2aa-2522226312ac" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371600 1081 "\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371600 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371600 1084 #uuid "5f70dac8-847a-5a3c-afa9-5b5ad69de949" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371601 1081 "\\frac{7}{4}\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371601 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371601 1084 #uuid "2c00a4c0-f033-55e1-9d1b-40d157b2fcff" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371602 1081 "\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{m/s}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371602 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371602 1084 #uuid "e6aeaa69-cb2d-572c-ad4b-0228aa3f284a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371603 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371604 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371603 1069 "q-116047" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371603 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371603 1071 "![](images/eb/eb0c6490a6e587b0d20b10a281584748d9367f2aa53a09159f6703cacbb632bb.png)\n\nIf the diagonals of a square increase at a rate of $9\\sqrt{2}\\text{ cm}\\text{/s}$, at what rate is the perimeter changing?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371603 1072 #uuid "dfd63c4d-025e-51b8-902f-535759a73c4e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371603 1074 "Let $p$ be the perimeter of the square, and $h$ be the length of the diagonal. The relationship between $p$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\np=2\\sqrt{2}h.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}h}(2\\sqrt{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that each diagonal of the square is increasing at a rate of $9\\sqrt{2}\\text{ cm}\\text{/s},$ so we have \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=9\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information into the above expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}p}{\\text{d}t} & =(9\\sqrt{2})\\cdot (2\\sqrt{2})=36\\text{ cm/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of the square increases at $36\\text{ cm}/\\text{s}.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371604 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371605 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371604 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371606 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371604 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371607 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371604 