#edb/ref 17592186371618 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371617 1069 "q-116749" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371617 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371617 1071 "![](images/35/3518e235844a154f6fd680edd2a169d4ff3b9812dcc38bb86b658bfc6c5d6e35.png)\n\nOne of the panels is melted in a squared container and shrank in a way such that the area of the square decreases at a rate of $14\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}\\text{/min}.$ At what rate are the diagonals of the square decreasing when the diagonals are $7\\,\\text{m}$ each?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371617 1072 #uuid "8c720afe-b544-56e9-a395-2df3d9555233" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371617 1074 "Let $h$ and $A$ be the length of the diagonals and the area of the square, respectively. Using the Pythagorean theorem, it can be shown that the relationship between $A$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nWe want to find\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}h}(\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot h \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{h}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that $A$ decreases at a rate of $14\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}\\text{/min},$ so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we want to compute the rate of change of the diagonals when the diagonal has length $h=7.$ Substituting this information into our expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{7}\\cdot (-14) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =-2\\text{ m}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the diagonals of the square are decreasing at a rate of $2\\text{ m}\\text{/min}.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371619 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371620 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371621 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371622 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371623 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371623 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371618 1080 #uuid "4f5c8382-cbcf-5150-867e-47f0c3bc6001" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371619 1081 "12\\text{ m}\\text{/min}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371619 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371619 1084 #uuid "2284a2b3-fc7f-5b9e-9a7f-263500130be3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371620 1081 "8\\text{ m}\\text{/min}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371620 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371620 1084 #uuid "d46ea121-76b7-5e42-a528-349eedc162e4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371621 1081 "4\\text{ m}\\text{/min}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371621 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371621 1084 #uuid "802358e8-a5ea-5f38-b2c8-e41754b2eb5c" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371622 1081 "7\\text{ m}\\text{/min}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371622 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371622 1084 #uuid "99478701-ee69-54dc-88e0-47947cde817a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 tr