d}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-v, \\\\ u+2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-v \\\\ u\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $det(A)>0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371708 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371709 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371710 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371711 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371712 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371708 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371707 1080 #uuid "b211404b-8e46-5fe3-a810-eb0ddf38f3f3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371708 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371708 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371708 1084 #uuid "08090adf-a2d1-5e61-9ed0-7da111463256" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371709 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371709 1083 #e