6371748 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=0$ gives the point $(0,0)$\n- $c=1$ gives a circle of radius $1$\n- $c=4$ gives a parabola" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371748 1072 #uuid "ee3c74bd-cd07-5dd0-b26f-4b93aa9647b3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371748 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={c}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is $x=y=0,$ which gives the point $(0,0).$ So, I is true.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ which gives a circle of radius $1.$ So, II is true.\n\n- If $c=4,$ the level curve is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=16,$ which gives a circle of radius $4.$ So, III is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371750 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371751 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371752 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371753 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371754 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371753 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371749 1080 #uuid "1f4c2c44-ea9c-52ce-a441-c7c1c5f23e29" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371750 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371750 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371750 1084 #uuid "f991d876-0326-5c0a-8b2a-21654d5968e4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371751 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533450 175921860