edb/ref 17592186371838 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371837 1069 "q-140368" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371837 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371837 1071 "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nFind the acute angle between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal. Round the answer to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371837 1072 #uuid "9f59cd55-772f-5274-bf95-91872631734e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371837 1074 "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-1)}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x$ or any other non-zero vector that is parallel to ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$ \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x}{‖x‖\\,‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{\\sqrt{20}\\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}{\\sqrt{20}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\sqrt{\\frac{7}{10}})≈{33.21}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371839 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371840 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371841 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371842 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371843 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371840 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371838 1080 #uuid "5ecfeca9-04bb-5e8f-bcb9-dc591b831fbb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371839 1081 "{32.31}^{∘}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371839 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371839 1084 #uuid "550d2623-ba4e-5e2c-9904-6bbcbc6529fb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371840 1081 "{33.21}^{∘}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371840 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371840 1084 #uuid "01efa27a-cf84-5aa5-b2d0-c2e5a9400d33" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371841 1081 "{31.23}^{∘}"