 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-8+9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}|1|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =(2-(-1))\\cdot (3-1) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371894 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371895 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371896 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371897 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371898 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371896 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371893 1080 #uuid "f732fda0-f223-5e8e-9cd7-3bad366f7805" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371894 1081 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371894 1083 #e