[17592186371940 1072 #uuid "21e23291-6559-5eea-9b70-7fd00996880f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371940 1074 "We would like to find a rectangular region of the form\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δ & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v\\le d} \\\\  & ={(u,v)\\,:\\,a\\le u(x,y)\\le b,\\,\\,c\\le v(x,y)\\le d},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the equations of the left, right, bottom, and top sides are\n\n$$\nu(x,y)=a,\\,u(x,y)=b,\\,v(x,y)=c,\\,v(x,y)=d.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze the boundary of our region $D.$ \n\nRewriting the equations \n\n$$\nx=y,\\,x=5y,\\,x=\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}},\\,x=\\frac{7}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nby moving both variables $x$ and $y$ to the left-hand side, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{y}=1,\\,\\frac{x}{y}=5,\\,x{y}^{2}=2,\\,x{y}^{2}=7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if we put $u(x,y)=\\frac{x}{y}$ and $v(x,y)=x{y}^{2},$ we can define the transformation ${T}^{-1}$ as\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:(x,y)\\to (\\,\\frac{x}{y}\\,,\\,x{y}^{2}).\n$$\n\nTo find $T,$ we should express $x$ and $y$ in terms of $u$ and $v.$ Recall that we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}u=\\frac{x}{y} \\\\ v=x{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, $x=uy.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get \n\n$$\nv=u{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{3}=\\frac{v}{u}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}$ back into $x=uy,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx=u\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}=\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the transformation $T$ can be given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}v},\\,\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{v}{u}}).\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371942 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371943 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371944 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371945 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371941 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371946 13