,-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}f⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{(-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+({f}^{′}f)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(z)=1+{z}^{4},$ we obtain ${f}^{′}(z)=4{z}^{3}.$ So, finally, we conclude that our expression for the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+(4{z}^{3})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1+{z}^{4})\\sqrt{1+16{z}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371949 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371950 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371951 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371952 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371953 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371948 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371953 13194139533450 175921