torname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{f}^{′}f⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{(-f\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-f\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}+({f}^{′}f)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{f}^{2}+{f}^{2}({f}^{′})^{2}} \\\\  & =f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{z}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\cdot \\theta \\,{|}_{0}^{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f=\\operatorname{ln}⁡z,$ we obtain ${f}^{′}=\\frac{1}{z}.$ So, finally, we conclude that our expression for the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}f\\sqrt{1+({f}^{′})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{z})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}⁡z\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{{z}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371956 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371957 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371958 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371959 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371960 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371955 1079 #edb/ref 1759218637