uuid "f7d11e71-624f-5d42-b0d4-35656fd37c78" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371979 1081 "{(\\rho ,\\theta ,ϕ)\\,:\\,0\\le \\rho \\le 1,\\,0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi ,\\,0\\le ϕ\\le \\pi /2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371979 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371979 1084 #uuid "cfc50b75-dae8-5026-be62-d0554770a166" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371980 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371981 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371980 1069 "q-161869" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371980 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371980 1071 "Use a change of variables to calculate the area of the finite region $D$ in the first quadrant bounded by the following curves and lines.\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x},\\,y=\\frac{4}{x},\\,x={y}^{2},\\,x=3{y}^{2}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371980 1072 #uuid "f2acf3d8-4862-5fab-a9f5-360ef711c3dc" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371980 1074 "The area of the required region is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy.\n$$\n\nLet's define a transformation $T$ as follows: \n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}x(u,v) \\\\ y(u,v)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe'll assume this transformation maps some region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane to our region $D$ in the $xy$-plane.\n\nTo compute the required area, we will use the change of variables formula\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}dxdy={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\text{ }dudv,\n$$\n\n  \n\nwhere $\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}$ is the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T.$\n\nTo compute the required area, we proceed in five steps:\n\n**Step 1**: Find a suitable change of variables.\n\nNotice that we can rewrite the equations of our curves as follows:\n\n$$\nxy=1,\\,xy=4,\\,\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=1,\\,\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=3\n$$\n\nThis suggests the following change of variables:\n\n$$\nu=xy,\\,v=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}\n$$\n\nThis change of variables gives us the *inverse* function ${T}^{-1},$ that is\n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\\to [\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) \\\\ v(x,y)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Find $Δ,$ which is the image of $D$ under the action of ${T}^{-1}.$ \n\nWe substitute $u=xy$ into the equations of the first and second curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & xy=1\\,⟹\\,u=1 \\\\  & xy=4\\,⟹\\,u=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAnd we substitute $v=\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}$ into the equations of the third and fourth curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,v=1 \\\\  & \\frac{x}{{y}^{2}}=3\\,⟹\\,v=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our domain in the $uv$-plane is the following rectangle:\n\n$$\nΔ={(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le 4,\\,1\\le v\\le 3}\n$$\n\n![](images/2d/2d98eb2de472226d010fb633478f3662754679c2256e3fd3d06600a6599bc7f5.png)\n\n**Step 3**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)} & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂u}{∂x} & \\frac{∂u}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂v}{∂x} & \\frac{∂v}{∂y}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}y & x \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}} & -\\frac{2x}{{y}^{3}}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =-3v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Compute the Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T:$\n\nThe Jacobian determinant corresponding to $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}={(\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)})}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3v}.\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{∂(u,v)}{∂(x,y)}\\ne 0$ everywhere inside $Δ.$  In other words, $T$ has no critical points inside $Δ.$\n\n**Step 5**: Compute the required area.\n\nWe calculate the required area by performing the change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={∬}_{Δ}|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={∬}_{Δ}|-\\frac{1}{3v}|\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{∬}_{Δ}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}u\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,\\text{d}u{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{1}{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (4-1)\\cdot (\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371982 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371983 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371984 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371985 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371986 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371986 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371981 1080 #uuid "f77b7f7b-0f4d-55ec-986c-8391703e056e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371982 1081 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371982 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371982 1084 #uuid "401d1340-9f46-59c1-abfc-5071d62dc570" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371983 1081 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371983 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371983 1084 #uuid "3204bc80-8ab3-5312-ac12-252b1d788312" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371984 1081 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371984 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371984 1084 #uuid "545f9367-80fc-527f-b725-9577794d6914" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371985 1081 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371985 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371985 1084 #uuid "6d8e3cd4-7080-5e0f-b3c0-62f9a1c245aa" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371986 1081 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371986 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371986 1084 #uuid "2897d53d-b8f5-5abb-a72a-895d82c614bb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371987 1068 #edb/ref 17592186371988 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371987 1069 "q-161898" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371987 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371987 1071 "Consider the vector field $F=⟨z,\\,0,\\,x⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the paraboloid $z=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and the plane $z=1.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371987 1072 #uuid "71368570-4ef4-5d96-b173-947fce0b9458" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371987 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=1$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper paraboloid ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=z=9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-(9-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\cdot (-2x)-(0)\\cdot (-2y)+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(18x-2{x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}19x-2{x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower plane ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nSince the positive orientation is downward, the unit normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,0,-1⟩.$ As a result, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}⟨z,0,x⟩\\cdot ⟨0,0,-1⟩\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}-x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}19x-2{x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}-x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}18x-2{x}^{3}-2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371989 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371990 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371991 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371992 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1075 #edb/ref 17592186371993 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1079 #edb/ref 17592186371991 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371988 1080 #uuid "106248c3-5a77-5d72-aed7-25c25eb96f2f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371989 1081 "19x-2{x}^{3}+3{y}^{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371989 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371989 1084 #uuid "69acc573-b0b8-5874-aab1-a28efcd81a93" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371990 1081 "16x-x{y}^{2}+2{y}^{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186371990 1083 #edb/