,$ ${v}_{1}(x),$ ${v}_{2}(x),$ $a,$ and $b$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the region of integration $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{2},\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{2},\\,\\,{y}^{3}\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch the region. Since it is a type I region, we first sketch the projection onto the $xy$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nE={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{2},\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{2}}.\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/58/58a9056015b3dad91ec7ae64bff893c8c6c2cce6480c979545e423cbe105ef03.png)\n\nThen, the region $R$ is shown in the diagram below, where ${y}^{3}\\le z\\le 2.$\n\n![](images/2f/2fdd6a15b4ddadfc3ee24af5e35e2a87e9e963ceeefbf858b704d78ee0b78513.png)\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $R$ as a type III region and its projection $D$ onto the $xz$-plane as a type I *plane* region.\n\nTo visualize this, imagine firing an arrow through the region parallel to the $y$-axis and in the direction of increasing $y,$ as shown below.\n\n![](images/65/65da730d32f200b8f9da004ee8cf6b7e79095e323961f4a5b6dfa0bddeace42b.png)\n\nThe arrow enters the region through the left boundary and leaves through the right boundary:\n\n- The right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=(x,z),$ is\n\n$$\nz={y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,y=\\sqrt[3]{z}\n$$\n\n- The left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{z}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/17/1743f540a85fc1c266c84da8f34b2012516b7bbc98d113cf7c62ba3bba8173c1.png)\n\nWe now consider the projection $D$ as a type II plane region in the $xz$-plane with the top curve given by \n\n$$\nz=(\\sqrt[3]{2})^{3}=2.\n$$\n\n![](images/b7/b76bf84e1179bec6a1e8e357c6cc628eee95c1663e6f0ff375135612a6f275de.png)\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{2},\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{{y}^{3}}^{2}f(x,y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372063 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372064 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372065 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372066 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372067 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372064 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372062 1080 #uuid "4c5dce1a-3fe0-5342-9853-86a9f1107b2a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372063 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt[3]{z+1}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372063 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372063 1084 #uuid "e0ee5b11-3727-53cc-bae8-700864970f3f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372064 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372064 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372064 1084 #uuid "55dcf7b1-a5b2-5d83-ba67-4bee831c3f62" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372065 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{{z}^{3}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372065 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372065 1084 #uuid "1371526b-5cd6-5f69-838b-b423ae77bc5b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372066 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{1}^{{z}^{3}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372066 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372066 1084 #uuid "3fc2bfc8-e5f7-5896-8f13-0b32aa42ac40" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372067 1081 "{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{2}}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}}f(x,y,z)\\,\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372067 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372067 1084 #uuid "e98b72b4-9900-5420-9208-7c8d7295e2ab" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372068 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372069 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372068 1069 "q-162518" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372068 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372068 1071 "Which of the following is a stream function for the vector field\n$F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j?$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372068 1072 #uuid "9fb4a1a9-80b2-5c9b-b44c-5418f559f461" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372068 1074 "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372070 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372071 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372072 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372073 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372074 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372073 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372069 1080 #uuid "337543b8-07ff-5870-85da-be792a9109dc" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372070 1081 "ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡xy" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372070 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 175