] [17592186372143 1081 "\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372143 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372143 1084 #uuid "17e65d6f-c15a-55b1-9a66-efebaf9391fe" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372144 1081 "\\frac{15}{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372144 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372144 1084 #uuid "210d794f-d0a6-51c4-91a0-389a72e11a32" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372145 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372146 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372145 1069 "q-162592" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372145 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372145 1071 "![](images/b2/b2c69c80570d6e35ac3f4b0d118230936b21a252161f8c6ef52ce12a43442621.png)\n\nThe curve ${C}_{1}$ has endpoints $A(5,1)$ and $B(2,4).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=-2y\\,i+{x}^{2}\\,j$ through ${C}_{1}$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector ${n}_{1},$ as shown above.\n\n*Hint: You're given that $F$ is source-free.*" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372145 1072 #uuid "af24040d-9174-5b76-b300-111cdbd02f2e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372145 1074 "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2},$ then the following are equivalent:\n\n- $F$ is a source-free vector field.\n\n- $∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.$\n\n- The flux ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s$ along any closed curve $C\\in D$ is zero.\n\n- Flux is path-independent. That is, given any two curves ${C}_{1},{C}_{2}\\in D$ with the same start and endpoints, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- There exists a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ for $F.$\n\nFirst, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-2y)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2})=0+0=0,\n$$\n\nwhich shows that $F$ is a source-free vector field.\n\nSince $F$ is source-free, we know the flux of $F$ is independent of the path. In particular,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s,\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{2}$ is the straight line from $A(5,1)$ to $B(2,4)$ and ${n}_{2}$ is its unit normal, shown in the diagram below. \n\n![](images/d1/d11be15ec3a455b3c19c52f64c767bbdd8bbd5eabf4c2243731eb5fc240b85d8.png)\n\nNotice that both ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotations of their respective unit tangent vectors.\n\nTo calculate the flux of $F$ across ${C}_{2},$ we will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo apply the formula,\n\n- the curve should be parametrized as $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ and\n\n- the unit normal vector ${n}_{2}$ *must* be a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of the unit normal tangent vector $T(t).$\n\nParametrizing ${C}_{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =5i+\\,j+t\\cdot [(2\\,i+4j)-(5i+\\,j)] \\\\  & =(-3t+5)\\,i+(3t+1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in [0,1].$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =-2y=-2(3t+1), \\\\ Q(x,y) & ={x}^{2}=(-3t+5)^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3t+5)=-3, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe evaluate the flux integral as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot {n}_{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-2(3t+1)\\cdot (3)-{(-3t+5)}^{2}\\cdot (-3)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(27{t}^{2}-108t+69)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[9{t}^{3}-54{t}^{2}+69t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(9-54+69) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot {n}_{1}\\,\\text{d}s=24.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372147 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372148 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372149 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372150 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372151 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372151 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372146 1080 #uuid "7ee18254-8e11-5d94-b582-cf41b03cdc04" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372147 1081 "28" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372147 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372147 1084 #uuid "b704a96f-535d-5e21-a89c-09d391dba585" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372148 1081 "-8" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372148 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372148 1084 #uuid "23fd46d2-0e94-5cdf-b124-36f1f705d0ec" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372149 1081 "15" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372149 1084 #uuid "68d3ddb7-3a94-543f-a12b-b24487df285d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372150 1081 "18" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372150 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372150 1084 #uuid "7744614f-0b13-52a0-9354-9749f239e72a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372151 1081 "24" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372151 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 1319413953345