c{∂Q}{∂y}=1+(-1)=0\n$$\n\n- Vector field II doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2+2y\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x{y}^{3},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2x{y}^{3}+4\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372175 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372176 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372177 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372178 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372179 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372177 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372174 1080 #uuid "1e54a2fc-4a8b-5cab-95e6-fb76489c0407" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372175 1081 "I, II, and III" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372175 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372175 1084 #uuid "838385c1-5d80-5fa7-887f-fb07eb950463" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372176 1081 "III and II only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372176 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372176 1084 #uuid "b248c3ba-148e-55e7-aa3d-4792ae3835b3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372177 1081 "I only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372177 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372177 1084 #uuid "29ac8e6a-e475-5224-9ac1-6d94bf491c44" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372178 1081 "III only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372178 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372178 1084 #uuid "8ee9dfb9-d450-58ba-8cf2-e32b997524ee" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372179 1081 "II only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372179 1084 #uuid "d706b176-5c95-5f54-8f51-91457ebb8721" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372180 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372181 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372180 1069 "q-162616" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372180 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372180 1071 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\n- $F(x,y)=y{e}^{x}\\,i+x{e}^{y}\\,j$\n- $F(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$\n- $F(x,y)={x}^{2}y\\,i-2y\\,j$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372180 1072 #uuid "28d6fde6-f5ac-58b4-8494-7d66bda4ef81" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372180 1074 "A vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each vector field.\n\n- Vector field I doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=y{e}^{x},\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =x{e}^{y}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=y{e}^{x}+x{e}^{y}\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II has a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III doesn't have a stream function. The partial derivatives are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2xy,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2xy+(-2)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372182 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372183 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372184 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372185 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372186 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372186 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372181 1080 #uuid "ab7199e8-3297-5917-9f13-01e35de9f6f0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372182 1081 "II and III only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372182 1084 #uuid "5a6ac29a-ed25-584f-9b59-c3bbc0c3e907" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372183 1081 "I only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372183 1084 #uuid "0ae883b1-9b1b-5317-a7ed-825acb737398" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372184 1081 "III only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372184 1084 #uuid "97635159-ede4-50a9-beb5-155e44a40dee" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372185 1081 "I and II only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372185 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372185 1084 #uuid "8c47f86a-7b1d-5f3f-81ff-fecdefe4c411" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372186 1081 "II only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372186 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372186 1084 #uuid "b9b676cb-dad2-558b-a0cb-d2d7177012b1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372187 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372188 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372187 1069 "q-162619" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372187 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372187 1071 "Determine the equation of the streamline that passes through the point $P(0,\\pi )$ for the vector field $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372187 1072 #uuid "dd6e61d1-6465-500e-9577-5af9c54bc069" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372187 1074 "The streamlines of a vector field are the level curves of its stream function and are tangential to the vector field at every point. \n\nIf $F$ represents the velocity field of a fluid flow, then they show the path traced out by a massless particle as it moves with the flow.\n. \n\nA vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ with a simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2}$ has a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ if and only if\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,i-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $F$ has a stream function, since\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+(-{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0.\n$$\n\nNext, we find a stream function. A function $ψ(x,y)$ is a stream function of the vector field $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ if \n\n$$\nP=\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y},\\,Q=-\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂ψ}{∂y}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,\\,\\frac{∂ψ}{∂x}={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nIntegrating these equations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+f(x),\\,ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y+g(y)\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are arbitrary functions. Finally, setting $f=g=0,$ we have\n\n$$\nψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y.\n$$\n\nFinally, we find the level curve of the stream function $ψ(x,y)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ that passes through $P.$\nFirst, we find the value of the stream function at $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(0,\\pi ) & ={e}^{(0)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the streamline that passes through $P(0,\\pi )$ is the $0$-level curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ψ(x,y) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our possible streamlines are $y=k\\pi $ for any integer $k.$ The streamline that passes through $P(0,\\pi )$ is $y=\\pi .$\nThe vector field and the streamline through the point $P$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/bd/bd732367a876d2e6bba6bf96728ebcf8430176d2f480bff30a054cac5389b1f2.png)" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372189 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372190 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372191 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372192 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372193 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372188 1077 "selection" 13194