lane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type I region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de82c9b30dfb156dea8ace88e27f00887dcecf197e7a50493f34f6a08dfae161.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $x=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-1|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=3M.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{1-{x}^{2}}|x-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{(x-1)^{2}}^{1-{x}^{2}}(x-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}[y]_{y=(x-1)^{2}}^{y=1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-1)^{2}(1-{x}^{2}-(x-1)^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{\\int }_{0}^{1}-2{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}+2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3M{[\\frac{-2{x}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{2}-2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =3M(-\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{3}{2}-2+1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372238 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372239 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372240 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372241 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372237 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372242 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372237 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 tr