e. Given that the region has an area of $\\frac{2}{3},$ find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=2.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372243 1072 #uuid "ec7b8780-df34-57c2-aa38-2856d08f105d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372243 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\le x\\le y},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a34ed2c8c25aa5c3c1e28e4458e11779f6b5948acbebdcb6e05b5bf1257689d4.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nSince the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{3M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{y}\\frac{3M}{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}/2}^{y}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}[x]_{x={y}^{2}/2}^{x=y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(y-2)^{2}(y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(-{y}^{4}+6{y}^{3}-12{y}^{2}+8y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}{[-\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{3{y}^{4}}{2}-4{y}^{3}+4{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{4}(-\\frac{32}{5}+24-32+16-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{6M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372244 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372245 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372244 1075 #edb/ref 175