& ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{[{x}^{2}y]}_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}(2-2{x}^{2}-1+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4k}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{15}{4}M{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}\\frac{15}{4}M{x}^{2}|x+1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}\\frac{15}{4}M{x}^{2}(x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}){\\int }_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})[y]_{1-{x}^{2}}^{2-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})(1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{6}-2{x}^{5}+2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M{[-\\frac{1}{7}{x}^{7}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{6}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M(-\\frac{2}{7}+0+0+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}M\\cdot \\frac{8}{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{10M}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372258 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372259 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372258 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372260 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372258 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372261 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372258 1075 #