 plate $D$ is $A=4\\cdot 6=24\\,{\\text{m}}^{2}.$\nSince the plate has a uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{6}{24}=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},\n$$\n\nand its center of mass is its centroid:\n\n$$\n(\\overset{¯}{x},\\overset{¯}{y})=(\\frac{-2+2}{2},\\frac{-3+3}{2})=(0,0)\n$$\n\nSince the center of mass is at the origin, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{1}{4}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{[{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=-3}^{y=3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}6{x}^{2}+18\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[2{x}^{3}+18x]_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(32+72) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(104) \\\\  & =26\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =26+(\\sqrt{3})^{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =26+18 \\\\  & =44\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372280 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372281 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372282 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372283 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372284 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372280 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372279 1080 #uuid "70cd93c3-949