can be expressed in polar coordinates as\n\n$$\nD={(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi }.\n$$\n\nSince the mass density is symmetric in $x$ and $y,$ the center of mass is at $(0,0).$ The mass density function, in polar coordinates, is given by \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{|r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta |}{r}=\\frac{1}{2}r|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|.\n$$\n\nNext, we find the mass of the plate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}r|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{r}^{3}{|}_{1}^{4}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(64-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =21\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =42\\,\\text{kg}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the moment of inertia about the perpendicular line through the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{M} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}r|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{r}^{4}\\,\\text{d}r\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}|\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )|\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{r}^{5}{|}_{1}^{4}\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(1024-1)\\cdot [-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1023}{5}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2046}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about a line $1\\,\\text{m}$ from the center of mass is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M \\\\  & =\\frac{2046}{5}+{1}^{2}\\cdot 42 \\\\  & =\\frac{2046}{5}+\\frac{210}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2256}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372322 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372323 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372324 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372325 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372326 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372322 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372321 1080 #uuid "57a3746b-e9fb-53da-9a01-e27a58b98aeb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372322 1081 "\\frac{2256}{5}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372322 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372322 1084 #uuid "23681ca2-8878-5cd9-8ca9-b76c979da2d1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372323 1081 "\\frac{1044}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372323 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372323 1084 #uuid "5f9020d3-0ee3-5b37-8a8a-9a18f42218a0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372324 1081 "\\frac{1023}{2}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372324 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372324 1084 #uuid "83140855-675b-59ea-8685-3c4f8b93ef7d" 13194139533450 17592186045585