 $x.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-7)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0-7)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{49}{9} & =1 \\\\ 9(x+3)^{2}+(49\\cdot 16) & =9\\cdot 16 \\\\ 9(x+3)^{2}+784 & =144 \\\\ 9(x+3)^{2} & =-640 \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =-\\frac{640}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x+3)^{2}\\ge 0$, there is no $x$ such that $(x+3)^{2}=-\\frac{640}{9}.$ Therefore, the ellipse has no $x$-intercepts, meaning that it does not intercept the $x$-axis at any point." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372336 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372337 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372338 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372339 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372340 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372337 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372335 1080 #uuid "c30b7192-6653-5671-97c2-bdcf6b73ca69" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372336 1081 "(\\pm 3,0)" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372336 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372336 1084 #uuid "d0292e86-12b7-5d98-9ba3-77441df6dd3c" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372337 1081 "There is no $x$-intercept" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372337 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372337 1084 #uuid "c18b6e15-f0e9-53ea-8a65-f790a079756f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372338 1081 "$(1,0)$ and $(2,0)$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372338 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [1759218637