"e7e32bdb-3f68-50ca-aa51-07df4959ce61" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372520 1081 "0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372520 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372520 1084 #uuid "33a0bfdd-adbe-52bd-bb36-4c921f95f34b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372521 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372522 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372521 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372521 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372521 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372522 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372521 1080 #uuid "dc1e5a25-eb92-528b-9252-5550cdc21086" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372522 1081 "2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372522 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372522 1084 #uuid "34d6b943-aeb2-5f7d-a297-cb064f81f755" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372524 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372526 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1069 "q-278376" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1071 "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}=16$ intersects the line $y=x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1072 #uuid "0e723854-969c-589a-8919-37b5f9cc49dd" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372523 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=x,$ we first replace $y$ with $x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ x & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-4$ and $x=4.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372524 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372525 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372524 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372524 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372524 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372525 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372524 1080 #uuid "d859565c-1c46-5d4e-aeee-eea75af73143" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372525 1081 "-4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372525 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372525 1084 #uuid "a9b5bc3e-ad12-5166-82da-040a2e0d2e64" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372526 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372527 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372526 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372526 1077 "field-2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372526 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372527 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372526 1080 #uuid "5c1a9d05-b1e4-5bb7-b347-f6fd96b39192" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372527 1081 "4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372527 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372527 1084 #uuid "bdad1af0-f941-54de-8b19-1c9467a05ec4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372529 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372531 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1069 "q-278377" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1071 "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $6{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=100$ intersects the line $y=-x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1072 #uuid "6416d497-4116-5214-ac5a-14a39d4c6414" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372528 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =100 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}-2(-x)^{2} & =100 \\\\ 6{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2} & =100 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =100 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =25 \\\\ x & =\\pm 5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-5$ and $x=5.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372529 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372530 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372529 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372529 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372529 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372530 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372529 1080 #uuid "e403a3da-e3be-5a86-9112-32c86069c6e9" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372530 1081 "-5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372530 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372530 1084 #uuid "641194c3-8dab-59b8-84a6-16f05c454989" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372531 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372532 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372531 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372531 1077 "field-2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372531 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372532 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372531 1080 #uuid "519b7a7e-edd2-52de-abee-4fb78a358b45" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372532 1081 "5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372532 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372532 1084 #uuid "896b220e-571e-594f-bb19-797bfdf2918b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372534 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372536 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1069 "q-278381" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1071 "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}=5$ intersects the line $y=2x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1072 #uuid "c152c9bf-68c4-5d51-815f-cda5cce8bb88" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372533 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=2x,$ we first replace $y$ with $2x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{(2x)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{8{x}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{6} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{5{x}^{2}}{6} & =5 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =6 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-\\sqrt{6}$ and $x=\\sqrt{6}.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372534 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372535 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372534 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372534 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372534 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372535 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372534 1080 #uuid "e5fc6b3f-e175-5782-806c-3339e4c6410d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372535 1081 "-\\sqrt{6}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372535 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372535 1084 #uuid "32443935-d57f-5bfb-b217-60de5c97a079" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372536 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372537 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372536 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372536 1077 "field-2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372536 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372537 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372536 1080 #uuid "a698358e-d765-57a0-8d12-66422fc5317d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372537 1081 "\\sqrt{6}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372537 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372537 1084 #uuid "85507a61-60eb-56e7-8b18-474b8245faeb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372539 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372541 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1069 "q-278382" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1071 "In **ascending order,** the $x$-coordinates of the points where the hyperbola ${y}^{2}-5{x}^{2}=16$ intersects the line $y=-3x$ are\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1072 #uuid "90bc2a2d-07d5-5376-a711-7ad916476cf8" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372538 1074 "To find the points where the hyperbola intersects the line $y=-3x,$ we first replace $y$ with $-3x$ in the equation of the hyperbola and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ (-3x)^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-5{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order, the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection are\n$x=-2$ and $x=2.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372539 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372540 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372539 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372539 1077 "field-2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372539 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372540 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372539 1080 #uuid "2755306b-4c03-5691-934c-6f333ac6ad69" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372540 1081 "2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372540 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372540 1084 #uuid "7897262f-d030-5071-88d7-f54e9e47cb1d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372541 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372542 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372541 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372541 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372541 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372542 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372541 1080 #uuid "dbde4724-febb-5d00-85ef-dd37718bad1d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372542 1081 "-2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372542 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372542 1084 #uuid "e2de7c64-00d8-52d9-b3c1-1f82fc5acfdd" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372543 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372544 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372543 1069 "q-278394" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372543 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372543 1071 "![](images/4b/4b669b8a0c02a57efe719666fe02d88d927cb3bab69cf9e7140596ae231be6b8.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372543 1072 #uuid "e11c278c-1ceb-507a-af93-ddaf25c18081" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372543 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,0),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372544 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372545 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372544 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372544 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372544 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372545 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372544 1080 #uuid "18235233-df1b-58b5-924f-f936658e4d66" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372545 1081 "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372545 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372545 1084 #uuid "37c8f6b8-ca20-5b2d-80c3-8c7ef1e6ec98" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372546 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372547 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372546 1069 "q-314495" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372546 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372546 1071 "The sides (in feet) of a square are increasing. At a particular moment, the rate of increase of the area of the square is numerically equal to seven times the rate of increase of the diagonals. What is the length $h$ of the diagonal of the square at that moment?\n\n$h=$\n{{field-1}} $\\text{ft}$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372546 1072 #uuid "d06153ec-06de-5e08-a5e0-36bc3ef9e7e2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372546 1074 "Let $A$ be the area of the square, and $h$ be the length of the diagonal. The relationship between $A$ and $h$ is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}h}(\\frac{{h}^{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe given information tells us that $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=7\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}$, so replacing $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ in the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =h\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ 7\\cancel{\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}} & =h\\cancel{\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}} \\\\ 7 & =h.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo at that particular moment, we have that the length of the diagonals of the square is $7\\,\\text{ ft}.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372547 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372548 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372547 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372547 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372547 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372548 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372547 1080 #uuid "6262049f-56fe-5753-8d3a-24cb4987048f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372548 1081 "7" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372548 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372548 1084 #uuid "66ffdd0c-16fb-5f50-b5ba-1cb07f13ccce" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372549 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372550 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372549 1069 "q-316568" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372549 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372549 1071 "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372549 1072 #uuid "76d159f6-fb9f-53b3-9d01-c808901cc326" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372549 1074 "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|4\\cdot 8-9\\cdot 7| \\\\  & =|32-63| \\\\  & =|-31| \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372550 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372551 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372550 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372550 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372550 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372551 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372550 1080 #uuid "046687d7-1553-5e3f-9041-80a23c24073b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372551 1081 "31" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372551 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372551 1084 #uuid "7f24d129-fc62-5693-8425-77de9cb5787e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372552 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372553 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372552 1069 "q-325141" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372552 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372552 1071 "![](images/31/3149b7dadc839e4155835c7cd0e9120a861dd79c698831e65b444a79d1ac7016.png)\n\nThe polar equation of the curve shown above is $r=${{field-1}}." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372552 1072 #uuid "c4380611-41b7-5b0c-ba84-23758b4a7c8e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372552 1074 "Notice that the given curve is a circle of radius $\\frac{19}{3}$ centered at the origin.\n\nTherefore, its polar equation is $r=\\frac{19}{3}.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372553 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372554 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372553 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372553 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372553 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372554 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372553 1080