d $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{′}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n5(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+10(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(10\\alpha +15\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(-15\\alpha +10\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}10\\alpha +15\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)) \\\\ -15\\alpha +10\\beta =7\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{21}{65},\\beta =\\frac{14}{65}.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{21}{65}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{14}{65}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny=A{e}^{-2x}+(-\\frac{21}{65})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+(\\frac{14}{65})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x).\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372635 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372636 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372635 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372635 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372635 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372636 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372635 1080 #uuid "22450113-bef0-5ee3-9f04-46ce4da4d68a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372636 1081 "-\\frac{21}{65}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372636 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372636 1084 #uuid "a9e3c48e-00c9-5f24-8582-80bc22d8e9f4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372637 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372638 13194139533450 1759218604558