ch step size in turn.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{2.5}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=2.5\\ge 2.$ Since this value falls outside the given region, Euler's method is not stable (or unstable) for this step size.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{0.6}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=0.6.$ Since this value falls within the given region,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & <\\lambda Δx<2 \\\\ 0 & <0.6<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEuler's method must be stable for this step size.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{3}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=3\\ge 2.$ Since this value falls outside the given region, Euler's method is not stable (or unstable) for this step size.\n\n- For $Δx=\\frac{1.9}{\\lambda },$ we have $\\lambda Δx=1.9.$ Since this value falls within the given region,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & <\\lambda Δx<2 \\\\ 0 & <1.9<2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEuler's method must be stable for this step size.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372671 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372672 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372673 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372674 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372675 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372671 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372670 1080 #uuid "bb9da5e8-498c-5b5c-9272-e68780e7c71e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372671 1081 "I and III only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372671 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372671 1084 #uuid "b35db7aa-7f9a-5f48-9dbd-2f97b5cff35d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372672 1081 "II and IV only" 1319