\\frac{(1.35)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{449}{800}| \\\\  & =0.561\\,25<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the modified Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=3.6,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(3.6)| & =|1-3.6+\\frac{(3.6)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{97}{25}| \\\\  & =3.88>1.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *outside* the stability region, the modified Euler method is unstable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.25)| & =|1-1.25+\\frac{(1.25)^{2}}{2}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{17}{32}| \\\\  & =0.531\\,25<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n Since this value falls *within* the stability region, the modified Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only\".\n\nNote that the stability region of the modified Euler method is $0<\\lambda Δx<2,$ so it is not absolutely stable." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372692 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372693 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372694 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372695 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372696 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372694 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372691 1080 #uuid "0fef6af3-965d-593f-a631-acf4aa6019ff" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372692 1081 "II and IV only" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372692 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372692 1084 #uuid "bcc749fa-fb45-52fe-abf6-a01153952b07" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372693 1081 "I, III, and IV only" 13194139533450 1759