/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372793 1084 #uuid "83820c0d-0a83-57e5-b5c4-09ed20e945d2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372794 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372795 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372794 1069 "q-341286" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372794 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372794 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ for $x\\in [0,\\pi ).$ The Fourier cosine series of the **even** $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the expression for ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372794 1072 #uuid "cb9e13e0-887f-5b9e-8044-67889d5c34d5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372794 1074 "For our Fourier cosine series, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})$ for $x\\in (0,\\pi ).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }{[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372795 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372796 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372795 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372795 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372795 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372796 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372795 1080 #uuid "0b583b62-1c51-5b30-9ea5-d6122f3390f0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372796 1081 "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372796 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372796 1084 #uuid "47130356-e22d-5712-aa39-331a07e435c6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372797 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372798 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372797 1069 "q-341788" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372797 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372797 1071 "$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi }{3}x)\n$$\n\nLet $F(x)=4{x}^{2}-6x+3$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ The Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension $f(x)$ of $F(x)$ is shown above. Find the exact value of ${a}_{0}.$\n\n${a}_{0}=$ {{field-1}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372797 1072 #uuid "7cfbfb37-8e3e-5c3d-8267-64ce726f2c24" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372797 1074 "For the Fourier series of a $2L$-periodic function, the constant term is given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{L}{\\int }_{-L}^{L}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and $f(x)=4{x}^{2}-6x+3$ for $x\\in [-3,3).$ So, substituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(4{x}^{2}-6x+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+3x]}_{-3}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot {3}^{3}-3\\cdot {3}^{2}+3\\cdot 3)-(\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot (-3)^{3}-3\\cdot (-3)^{2}+3\\cdot (-3))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(18-(-72)) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372798 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372799 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372798 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372798 1077 "field-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372798 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372799 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372798 1080 #uuid "3cb42d37-67e0-5792-9f61-4d03