constant of proportionality $L=6\\,\\text{H}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=6\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, these values are related by the equation\n\n$$\n15=30I+500q+6\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $t,$ the differential equation governing the current in the circuit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dt}(15) & =\\frac{d}{dt}(30I+500q+6\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}) \\\\ 0 & =30\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+500\\,\\frac{dq}{dt}+6\\,\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, when substituting in $I=\\frac{dq}{dt},$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+5\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+\\frac{250}{3}I=0.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372954 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372955 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372956 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372957 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372958 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372956 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372953 1080 #uuid "19645aa4-ddb3-5e95-bb80-40475bc2ac61" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372954 1081 "\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+30\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+\\frac{250}{3}I=0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372954 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372954 1084 #uuid "ea061ac6-2b6e-507f-9cec-6e521b4ed617" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372955 1081 "\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+5\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+500=0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372955 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372955 1084 #uuid "37d62393-54d4-5bc1-971e-d68fc9a2f895" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372956 1081 "\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+5\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+\\frac{250}{3}I=0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372956 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372956 1084 #uuid "bdcdbc5d-a212-556d-bcef-1fc3f03c1eae" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372957 1081 "\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+5\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+\\frac{250}{3}I=15" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372957 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372957 1084 #uuid "c043242b-b393-5f63-b67c-0fe8df89b2c1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372958 1081 "\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+30\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+500I=0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372958 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372958 1084 #uuid "39cc0660-2f8d-5b41-88a6-39866a217e06" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372959 1068 #edb/ref 17592186372960 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372959 1069 "q-345287" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372959 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372959 1071 "![](images/5d/5decb376a08854254c72dc477de747210f462643893fdd060eb75b63c943981c.png)\n\nConsider the RCL circuit shown above. Given that the current $I(t)$ in the circuit at time $t$ seconds is given by\n\n$$\nI(t)=A{e}^{-2t}+B{e}^{-t}+\\frac{P}{26}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{Q}{26}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B,$ $P,$ and $Q$ are constants, find the value of $P+Q.$\n\n*Hint: The voltage drop ${V}_{C}$ across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C},$ where $C$ is the capacitance measured in Farads.*" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372959 1072 #uuid "55652e08-5105-537a-9ced-61b36f53413d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372959 1074 "The diagram shows a series RCL circuit with a source electromotive force (EMF) of $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\,\\text{V},$ a resistor of resistance $3\\,Ω,$ a capacitor of capacitance $0.5\\,\\text{F},$ and an inductor of inductance $1\\,\\text{H}.$\n\nThe current $I,$ measured in amperes, is defined as the rate of flow of charge $q,$ measured in coulombs.\n\n$$\nI=\\frac{dq}{dt}\n$$\n\nKirchhoff's voltage law states that in a series circuit, the source voltage (EMF) equals the sum of the voltage drops.\n\nIn an RCL circuit, there are three voltage drops:\n\n- The voltage drop across the resistor is proportional to the current, with a constant of proportionality $R=3\\,Ω.$ So,\n\n$$\n{V}_{R}=3I.\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the capacitor is related to its charge by $q=C{V}_{C}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{V}_{C}=\\frac{q}{C}=\\frac{q}{0.5}=2q.\n$$\n\n- The voltage drop across the inductor is proportional to the rate of change of current, with a constant of proportionality $L=1\\,\\text{H}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{V}_{L}=1\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by Kirchhoff's voltage law, these values are related by the equation\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)=3I+2q+1\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $t,$ the differential equation governing the current in the circuit is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d}{dt}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =\\frac{d}{dt}(3I+2q+1\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}) \\\\ 15\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) & =3\\,\\frac{dI}{dt}+2I+1\\,\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, when substituting in $I=\\frac{dq}{dt},$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{{d}^{2}I}{d{t}^{2}}+3\\cdot \\frac{dI}{dt}+2I=15\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nThe given equation is a second-order linear equation with constant coefficients. To find the general solution, we must sum the complementary and particular solutions.\n\n- To find the complementary solution ${I}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{d}^{2}{I}_{c}}{d{t}^{2}}+3\\cdot \\frac{d{I}_{c}}{dt}+2{I}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving using an integration technique, such as a trial solution, we obtain the complementary solution\n\n$$\n{I}_{c}(t)=A{e}^{-2t}+B{e}^{-t},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are constants.\n\n- Next, we find a particular solution. Note that the right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is sinusoidal with argument $3t.$ So, we assume that the particular solution is also sinusoidal with argument $3t,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{I}_{p}(t)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute this, as well as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{d{I}_{p}}{dt} & =-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t), \\\\ \\frac{{d}^{2}{I}_{p}}{d{t}^{2}} & =-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ninto the inhomogeneous equation and group like terms on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-9\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-9\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))+3(-3\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+3\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))\\,\\,\\, \\\\ +2(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =15\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ (-7\\alpha +9\\beta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+(-9\\alpha -7\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =15\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-7\\alpha +9\\beta =15\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)) \\\\ -9\\alpha -7\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{21}{26}$ and $\\beta =\\frac{27}{26}.$ Therefore, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{I}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{21}{26}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{27}{26}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nI(t)={I}_{c}(t)+{I}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-2t}+B{e}^{-t}-\\frac{21}{26}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+\\frac{27}{26}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $P=-21$ and $Q=27,$ and\n\n$$\nP+Q=-21+27=6.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372961 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372962 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372963 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372964 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1075 #edb/ref 17592186372965 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1079 #edb/ref 17592186372963 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372960 1080 #uuid "b6e69995-c548-5f93-8c1d-fa4941ec6350" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372961 1081 "12" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372961 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372961 1084 #uuid "96430721-ff82-5dda-8fe7-0d3cef7072a0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372962 1081 "8" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372962 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372962 1084 #uuid "9e49753b-a01f-54c2-b365-3027abf14211" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372963 1081 "6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372963 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372963 1084 #uuid "139fe288-aca4-58ef-8955-deb101c23234" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372964 1081 "4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372964 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372964 1084 #uuid "850b3bce-f8aa-55fd-84aa-85b5d60a1197" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372965 1081 "-6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186372965 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 1