x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373119 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373120 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373121 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373122 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373123 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373122 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373118 1080 #uuid "884e0837-dc25-582c-8453-afd1b56b7ce5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373119 1081 "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373119 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373119 1084 #uuid "56a80b40-83c9-5a0c-b8de-49c06e672fc1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373120 1081 "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{2}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373120 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373120 1084 #uuid "2d6ecce1-0166-520e-8732-da9a869f6972" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373121 1081 "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373121 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373121 1084 #uuid "490d76a9-1c74-52a1-970d-53ccf9e78a74" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373122 1081 "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373122 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373122 1084 #uuid "dfc9510a-1fe8-5c2a-8999-5d24f75e147e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373123 1081 "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{9}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373123 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373123 1084 #uuid "01dfe7f3-e59a-58b3-98eb-dce687463c7f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373124 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373125 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373124 1069 "q-71222" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373124 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373124 1071 "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {e}^{u}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=4t-3,$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373124 1072 #uuid "df22d5ba-b0c3-58b3-a878-bdf0e607174d" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373124 1074 "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ {e}^{u}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-3)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ {e}^{u(t)}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ {e}^{4t-3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373126 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373127 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373128 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373129 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373130 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373128 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373125 1080 #uuid "91cea048-4a27-504b-b918-c58dbf7788d6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373126 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373126 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373126 1084 #uuid "e2353783-74f2-5934-bfba-3023b84ceef4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373127 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373127 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373127 1084 #uuid "9fe13228-3768-591d-9f6a-24b6e1eb93a1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373128 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 4{e}^{4t-3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373128 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373128 1084 #uuid "72be2dff-28b8-52fc-9246-55ec88b83a57" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373129 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ 8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373129 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373129 1084 #uuid "61bb40c2-9ecf-585d-b790-f34cbaa9de79" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373130 1081 "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t-3) \\\\ {e}^{4t-3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373130 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373130 1084 #uuid "243cbcf4-b0d8-5b82-ad87-04f8e247276b" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373131 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373132 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373131 1069 "q-71394" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373131 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373131 1071 "Consider the plane curve $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}=1.$  Find the equation of the normal line to the curve at the point $(0,4).$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373131 1072 #uuid "03866640-0a40-5a70-8301-d2aa021aa524" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373131 1074 "If we set $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=1.$  \n\nA normal vector to the level curve that passes through the point $(0,4)$ can be found by computing $∇f(0,4).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(0,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9})\\,i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9})\\,j \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{9}x\\,i+\\frac{1}{8}y\\,j \\\\ ∇f(0,4) & =-\\frac{2}{9}(0)\\,i+\\frac{1}{8}(4)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,j \\\\  & =⟨0,\\frac{1}{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(0,4)=⟨0,\\frac{1}{2}⟩$ is a normal vector to the curve at $(0,4).$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-{x}_{0}){v}_{y}-(y-{y}_{0}){v}_{x} & =0 \\\\ (x-0)\\frac{1}{2}-(y-4)0 & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373133 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373134 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373135 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373136 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373137 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373135 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373132 1080 #uuid "c09f18f3-dc2a-5860-86fe-1086c3a20b7a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373133 1081 "y=4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373133 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373133 1084 #uuid "23d40bef-5cc1-533e-a776-8178968f8226" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373134 1081 "x=4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373134 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373134 1084 #uuid "8b5e25f1-f9d6-5abd-be1b-a979b00ae356" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373135 1081 "x=0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373135 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373135 1084 #uuid "f370372e-718e-527d-b206-115386ee2633" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373136 1081 "y=0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373136 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373136 1084 #uuid "0c3b4fbb-9302-5aaa-8ef1-476b737ddbbd" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373137 1081 "x-y=-4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373137 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373137 1084 #uuid "a9003cf3-3b04-543a-a41c-c583ef479eb1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373138 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373139 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373138 1069 "q-71402" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373138 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373138 1071 "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=9x+3y-4$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $c=0$ gives an ellipse\n- $c=-4$ gives a line\n- $c=5$ gives a hyperbola" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373138 1072 #uuid "c853fbcf-5be0-5101-8f2a-558cbd4a782f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373138 1074 "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9x+3y-4 & =c \\\\ 3y & =-9x+c+4 \\\\ y & =-3x+\\frac{c+4}{9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+\\frac{4}{9},$ which is not an ellipse.\n\n- If $c=-4$ then the level curve is $y=-3x,$ which is a line.\n\n- If $c=5$ then the level curve is $y=-3x+3,$ which is not a hyperbola.\n\nSo, only statement II is true." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373140 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373141 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373142 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373143 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373144 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373139 1079 #edb/ref 1