iewed as the level surface $f(x,y,z)=3.$ \n\nA normal vector to the level surface that passes through the point $(-1,-1,1)$ can be found by computing $∇f(-1,-1,1).$ \n\nSo, we find the gradient and evaluate it at $(-1,-1,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\text{ }j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})k \\\\  & =2x\\text{ }i+2y\\text{ }j+2z\\text{ }k \\\\ ∇f(-1,-1,1) & =2(-1)\\text{ }i+2(-1)\\text{ }j+2(1)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =-2\\,i-2\\,j+2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the Cartesian equation of the line that is parallel to $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$ and passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be written as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}} \\\\ \\frac{x-(-1)}{-2}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{-2}=\\frac{z-1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+1}{-2}=\\frac{y+1}{-2}=\\frac{z-1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{x+1}{1}=\\frac{y+1}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{-1} \\\\ x+1=y+1=\\frac{z-1}{-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373147 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373148 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373149 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373150 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373151 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373151 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373146 1080 #uuid "31f112b8-6ada-53ff-b6b3-be00d57b76b2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373147 1081 "x-1=y+1=\\frac{z-1}{-1}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373147 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373147 1084 #uuid "fd12d1d6-f236-57c3-bd6d-b0a476bef5f3" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373148 1081 "x+1=y+1=\\frac{z+1}{-1}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373148 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373148 1084 #uuid "e0818182-cafe-552e-a4a0-98b0c1314881" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373149 1081 "x+1=y-1=z-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373149 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373149 1084 #uuid "df5c957f-327c-59b5-a275-854f61c6c1b1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373150 1081 "x+1=y+1=z-1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373150 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373150 1084 #uuid "4643467a-d570-58d2-ac66-45f1f209b1ac" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373151 1081 "x+1=y+1=\\frac{z-1}{-1}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373151 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373151 1084 #uuid "c777726a-c485-5a89-bead-338bff4761cc" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373152 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373153 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373152 1069 "q-7163" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373152 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373152 1071 "The position vector $r$ of a particle $P$ (relative to a fixed origin $O$) at time $t$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4}+18,\\,\\frac{(2t-1)(t+8)}{4}⟩.\n$$\n\nCalculate the acceleration vector $a.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373152 1072 #uuid "7c40e900-4168-58d0-bff9-0089fc2f1abd" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373152 1074 "To compute the acceleration vector, we need to differentiate the velocity vector. So first, we need to compute the velocity vector, which we can do this by differentiating the position vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4}+18),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{(2t-1)(t+8)}{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{t}{2},\\,\\frac{2\\cdot (t+8)+(2t-1)\\cdot 1}{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{t}{2},\\,\\frac{4t+15}{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4t+15}{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373154 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373155 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373156 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373157 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373158 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373157 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373153 1080 #uuid "4539d153-f460-5844-a172-6c13c9d37598" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373154 1081 "a=⟨1,\\,1⟩" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373154 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373154 1084 #uuid "26dda759-d8c8-506b-aa59-49eec2f18e9e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373155 1081 "a=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{t}{4}⟩" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373155 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373155 1084 #uuid "d