172 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373172 1084 #uuid "4b187e20-0d76-5b76-bb07-602904c533d9" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373173 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373174 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373173 1069 "q-71980" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373173 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373173 1071 "Write the complex number $z=\\sqrt{3}+3\\text{i}$ in exponential form." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373173 1072 #uuid "b8e250fb-bb22-5fa7-a996-d9a2f566f848" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373173 1074 "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373175 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373176 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373177 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373178 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373179 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373175 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373174 1080 #uuid "a8dd0ad5-380d-539e-8b6f-2013fb067c0a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373175 1081 "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373175 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373175 1084 #uuid "da888f4e-6ea2-5797-9fad-27364fa17794" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373176 1081 "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373176 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373176 1084 #uuid "c27d8ed3-781c-5ca4-8106-6fd6792152c7" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373177 1081 "z=3\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373177 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373177 1084 #uuid "46ce225e-2367-5d7f-be68-c7247ca63e5f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373178 1081 "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/6}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373178 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373178 1084 #uuid "9cd1a88b-d9fa-56fd-a7d3-096a1437006a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373179 1081 "z=3\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373179 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373179 1084 #uuid "0b2c5cc0-3b42-5d6e-bc78-cb94824b6dc0" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373180 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373181 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373180 1069 "q-72143" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373180 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373180 1071 "![](images/76/768046952484d181a404486547db84882424d98da4f677254484e1083580a39b.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373180 1072 #uuid "ef441fce-64e9-5f90-b9fb-0d44af6b333e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373180 1074 "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=y$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$ So, we have $0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/d5/d55cb7ea67d9865368c744577bb4a4b22a3635e8e62869ee65e945612d6c0e98.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=y$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt{y}.$ So, we have $y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373182 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373183 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373184 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373185 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373186 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373182 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373181 1080 #uuid "257fac2f-8a02-59c7-aca1-ef19cbb1795a" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373182 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373182 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373182 1084 #uuid "6a975ac4-7eb7-5fd7-877f-3b02d86d178c" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373183 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 1}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373183 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373183 1084 #uuid "39895c7e-c47a-544c-91d0-9dfd7ed83606" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373184 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le y}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373184 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373184 1084 #uuid "a9081b22-1a7d-5fe6-a42e-28c78f31adb1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373185 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373185 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373185 1084 #uuid "cdc5c900-890c-5102-b2c4-66ae4d181695" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373186 1081 "D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373186 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373186 1084 #uuid "9ec0e614-7e69-564e-8bef-ca2ee0f86847" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373187 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373188 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373187 1069 "q-72251" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373187 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373187 1071 "![](images/82/8289d16711c1ce0a97e056b44acd949908ed97ce6ae2e4c68d1e5b9022846d01.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373187 1072 #uuid "f15691a7-e2ba-5a41-93ce-4813f75267cf" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373187 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-3,2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373189 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373190 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373191 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373192 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373193 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373190 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373188 1080 #uuid "630a029c-6e06-5fd5-84a7-4a8213f014cb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373189 1081 "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{25}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373189 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373189 1084 #uuid "6805f839-3bcd-57e0-afc7-fccf7bbdeae6" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373190 1081 "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{25}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373190 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373190 1084 #uuid "2365b4a0-4a4e-5c09-8c6f-06c3940e1f92" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373191 1081 "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{10}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373191 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373191 1084 #uuid "1389bd33-3c64-5352-8c10-4e2a1ccf402e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373192 1081 "\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{10}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373192 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373192 1084 #uuid "50ed5beb-40df-5cbb-b518-b7088703743f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373193 1081 "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{25}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373193 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373193 1084 #uuid "a7318fc4-07ec-5dda-9f48-5c543101ca23" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373194 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373195 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373194 1069 "q-73318" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373194 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373194 1071 "The area of a square decreases at a rate of $12\\,{\\text{in}}^{2}\\text{/min}.$ If $x$ and $A$ denote the side length and area of the square, respectively, then find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$, where $t$ is the time in minutes." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373194 1072 #uuid "e6f517ab-ab71-54a6-88e9-bc765cc4550f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373194 1074 "Here, the area is changing at a constant rate, and we want to know the rate at which the side lengths are changing.\n\nFirst, let's draw a diagram:\n\n![](images/f4/f4125cebd7553bb8b106a8baff39a6e4a120b9d9e5cdf2c4c9c0a9a676558897.png)\n\nWe want to find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ The area $A$ is related to side length $x$ by the formula\n\n$$\nA={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this relationship with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(A) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know from the given information that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-12\\text{ in}{}^{2}\\text{/min}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this information, we reach\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{6}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373196 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373197 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373198 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373199 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373200 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373197 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373195 1080 #uuid "b8b8ebc5-b1cb-51e5-ace6-4230ff06b936" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373196 1081 "-6x" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373196 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373196 1084 #uuid "0637a4d0-6b43-5e08-9f4b-cf24e433081c" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373197 1081 "-\\frac{6}{x}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373197 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373197 1084 #uuid "5c81e1aa-915b-5422-99f0-467b0e070289" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373198 1081 "\\frac{x}{6}" 1319413953