true] [17592186373228 1084 #uuid "0e98eacd-a3a2-500a-b565-dbdc2037ff58" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373229 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373230 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373229 1069 "q-76909" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373229 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373229 1071 "Find the arc length of the curve $r(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}+4,\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}⟩$\nfrom  $t=0$ to $t=4.$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373229 1072 #uuid "c6a58127-1393-5bb0-acf9-ab77e9d7ffad" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373229 1074 "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+4),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2t,\\,2t,\\,t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2t)}^{2}+{(2t)}^{2}+{(t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $t\\ge 0$ for $t\\in [0,4].$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}3t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}({t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373231 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373232 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373233 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373234 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373235 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373235 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373230 1080 #uuid "5f0cc1ce-5d3d-51df-bd70-280