matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373373 1072 #uuid "20c4ad19-4d9c-5e04-8446-e86474c33e0f" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373373 1074 "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](images/54/54bd0b8459c9acc3ad1212c39b20ebad55e0b20a38e1f943b861b8679f754225.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 4=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=3\\cdot 4-2\\cdot 5=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373375 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373376 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373377 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373378 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373379 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373377 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373374 1080 #uuid "1b5f44ff-78aa-58e2-96eb-17b0b037f669" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373375 1081 "12" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373375 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373375 1084 #uuid "0ca94297-4446-5915-bcbd-83ac04217874" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373376 1081 "20" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373376 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373376 1084 #uuid "b5fd3842-8057-5b8a-a22b-96df6f559ceb" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373377 1081 "16" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373377 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373377 1084 #uuid "c40ad2e5-9798-5758-946c-bab2442c9830" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373378 1081 "8" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373378 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373378 1084 #uuid "0dba79ad-9aa5-506a-98e2-99ed9771f8b5" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373379 1081 "4" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373379 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373379 1084 #uuid "d1203f77-4068-51ab-bdb5-37d0a3677f59" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373380 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373381 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373380 1069 "q-85314" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373380 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373380 1071 "Let $D$ be the finite region bounded by the curve \n$(x-y)^{2}+x+y=0$ and  the line $y=0.$ \nConsider the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (x(u,v),y(u,v)),\n$$\n\nwhere $u=x-y$ and $v=x+y.$ Find the representation of ${T}^{-1}(D)$ in the $uv$-plane." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373380 1072 #uuid "bb3932ad-6398-5142-9ae7-9ead5c34792e" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373380 1074 "First, notice that we are given that \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}x-y \\\\ x+y\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x-y=u$ and $x+y=v$ into the equation of the first curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-y)^{2}+x+y=0\\,⟹\\,(x-y)^{2}+(x+y)=0\\,⟹\\,v=-{u}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x-y=u \\\\ x+y=v\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{v-u}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this value into the equation of the given line yields:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=0\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{v-u}{2}=0 & \\,⟹\\,v=u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, to find the intersections of the resulting lines in the $uv$-plane, we solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}v=-{u}^{2} \\\\ v=u\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}u(u+1)=0 \\\\ v=u.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection points are $(0,0)$ and $(-1,-1).$ \n\n![](images/05/05d7e65dca3c6d116d01be9e57fc83f3e3edcda4135a3f96fea82af8db4f2d1e.png)\n\nAs a result, our domain in the $uv$-plane has the type I representation \n\n$$\n{T}^{-1}(D)={(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,u\\le v\\le -{u}^{2}}.\n$$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373382 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373383 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373384 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373385 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373386 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1077 "selection" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1079 #edb/ref 17592186373382 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373381 1080 #uuid "23350df3-f523-5ba3-82a1-2c19d5fe91f1" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373382 1081 "{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,u\\le v\\le -{u}^{2}}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373382 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373382 1084 #uuid "b13425c2-ab49-5777-adaa-78d980364d86" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373383 1081 "{(u,v)\\,:\\,-1\\le u\\le 0,\\,{u}^{2}\\le v\\le u}" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373383 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139533450 1759