"${x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373404 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373404 1084 #uuid "048a936f-1725-5c13-bea4-65127ef9eac2" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373405 1081 "${x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{x}_{2}$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373405 1083 #edb/ref 17592186045500 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373405 1084 #uuid "c6086673-4988-5e1a-af21-82e3b6fdac99" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373406 1068 #edb/ref 17592186373407 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373406 1069 "q-9460" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373406 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373406 1071 "Calculate the point where the ellipse  ${x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}x+8y+2=0$ intercepts the $x$-axis." 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373406 1072 #uuid "f3d479ad-dea6-5bd5-bf45-761d1d1ac539" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373406 1074 "To calculate the $x$-intercepts, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the ellipse and solve the resulting equation for $x.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}x+8y+2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\cdot {0}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}x+8\\cdot 0+2 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2\\sqrt{2}x+2 & =0 \\\\ (x+\\sqrt{2})^{2} & =0 \\\\ x+\\sqrt{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $x$-axis at $(-\\sqrt{2},0).$" 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373408 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373409 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373410 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373411 13194139533450 17592186045585 true] [17592186373407 1075 #edb/ref 17592186373412 1319